⚡🇮🇷🇨🇳 Iran is set to receive its first shipment of 300–400 Chinese-made MANPADS within weeks, according to Reuters. The $60–70 million deal covers QW-12 and FN-16 shoulder-fired missile systems designed to engage low-flying aircraft, drones, and helicopters.

Deliveries are expected to be flown from Urumqi, China, and transited through Pakistan — though Islamabad denies involvement. Beijing has called the reports “completely baseless.”

